                  "Migration cases are cases related to foreign nationals and citizenship, and they are handled by the migration courts at the administrative courts in Gothenburg, Malmö, Luleå, and Stockholm. In some years, a few migration cases may also occur at another administrative court even though it is not a migration court. In 2006, the migration courts and the Migration Court of Appeal were established as lower and higher instances in migration cases. Prior to this, decisions by the Swedish Migration Agency were appealed to the Aliens Appeals Board, and historical data from the cases of the Aliens Appeals Board was transferred to the new migration courts. However, the migration court in Luleå was not established until October 1, 2013."
